{"name":"Golden Guernsey","hex":"#e1c3bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"guernsey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A seaman's knitted woolen sweater, similar to a jersey.","The shirt worn by the players."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guernsey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Guernsey","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden Guernsey is a rare breed of dairy goat from Guernsey in the Channel Islands, where it has been known for more than two hundred years. In 2024 it received a Royal title from King Charles III and is officially the Royal Golden Guernsey Goat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Golden_Guernsey_goats.jpg/330px-Golden_Guernsey_goats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Guernsey","wikidata":"Q1393542"},{"title":"Guernsey","blocks":[{"text":"Guernsey is the second-largest island in the Channel Islands, located 27 miles (43 km) west of the Cotentin Peninsula, Normandy. It is the largest island in the Bailiwick of Guernsey, which includes five other inhabited islands – Alderney, Herm, Jethou, Brecqhou and Sark – and many small islets and rocks. The bailiwick has a population of 63,950, the vast majority of whom live on Guernsey, and the island has a land area of 24 square miles (62 km2)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Guernsey-Guernsey.png/330px-Guernsey-Guernsey.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik